709
00:28:29.467 --> 00:28:33.848
<v GAUTHIA>But I can remember kinfolks was doing it and Mama didn't like that.

710
00:28:33.848 --> 00:28:34.185
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

711
00:28:34.185 --> 00:28:36.880
<v GAUTHIA>She always wanted to make me feel good.

712
00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:39.576
She say, "Judy, you got some good hair."

713
00:28:39.576 --> 00:28:44.967
And honey baby, I did not have no good hair. [laughs] I had some nappy hair.

714
00:28:44.967 --> 00:28:46.989
I can remember crying many days.

715
00:28:46.989 --> 00:28:48.000
<v DIGILORMO>Oh, no.

716
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:51.030
<v GAUTHIA>When they'd comb that tangle out it would be, "Ahh!

717
00:28:51.030 --> 00:28:51.636
It hurts!

718
00:28:51.636 --> 00:28:52.242
It hurts!"

719
00:28:52.242 --> 00:28:53.758
Type of thing like that.

720
00:28:53.758 --> 00:28:58.000
And I liked it when Sally would comb my hair because she would comb

721
00:28:58.000 --> 00:28:58.606
<c.p>me pretty.

722
00:28:58.606 --> 00:29:03.152
And where my parents and my mother would comb it, two big old horse plaits.

723
00:29:03.152 --> 00:29:04.061
Stuff like that.

724
00:29:04.061 --> 00:29:08.303
She didn't really worry about trying to fix it to look cute type thing.

725
00:29:08.303 --> 00:29:10.121
But Sally would hurt my hair.

726
00:29:10.121 --> 00:29:11.636
She would be pulling it.

727
00:29:11.636 --> 00:29:14.667
She'd say, "Girl, you want me to comb your hair?

728
00:29:14.667 --> 00:29:16.182
Be still and hush up."

729
00:29:16.182 --> 00:29:18.000
So I can remember that.

730
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:18.667
<v DIGILORMO>You tender-headed?

731
00:29:18.667 --> 00:29:22.333
<v GAUTHIA>I really wasn't tender-headed, but it just would hurt a lot.

732
00:29:22.333 --> 00:29:23.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

733
00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:26.034
<v GAUTHIA>No, I don't think I was ever tender-headed.

734
00:29:26.034 --> 00:29:28.310
It’s just, that's what I said.

735
00:29:28.310 --> 00:29:33.241
My hair [?] was totally different from Mama's, and Sally's, and my brother's, too.

736
00:29:33.241 --> 00:29:40.069
I would say all the time my daddy hair wasn't . . . It’s turned straight now since he's gotten older,

737
00:29:40.069 --> 00:29:45.000
but I say we took after Daddy's . . . And it was Nelson and myself.

738
00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:48.793
And Alvin and Allen tooked after my mama’s straighter hair.

739
00:29:48.793 --> 00:29:51.069
They had some good stuff, so.

740
00:29:51.069 --> 00:29:53.724
I'm proud of my hair, though. [laughs]

741
00:29:53.724 --> 00:29:54.103
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

742
00:29:54.103 --> 00:29:56.000
I like your hair.

743
00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:04.078
<v GAUTHIA>But Mama really would say I had some good hair just like her and Sally and I couldn't figure that out for nothing in the world.

744
00:30:04.078 --> 00:30:10.602
I said to myself, "I'm the only one that be crying," [laughs] because I had some tangles and stuff like that.

745
00:30:10.602 --> 00:30:18.369
My cousin, they wanted to press my hair and Mama didn't care for me to do that because she thought, "Oh, that's going to mess

746
00:30:18.369 --> 00:30:19.301
<c.p>your hair up."

747
00:30:19.301 --> 00:30:19.612
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

748
00:30:19.612 --> 00:30:22.097
<v GAUTHIA>No, they was trying to help my hair.

749
00:30:22.097 --> 00:30:27.379
Make it easier for me to comb it, or they comb it and stuff like that but . . .

750
00:30:27.379 --> 00:30:28.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

751
00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:33.778
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah, so she really wanted me to feel special on my hair, but I knew better.

752
00:30:33.778 --> 00:30:34.139
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

753
00:30:34.139 --> 00:30:35.222
<v GAUTHIA>Yes indeed, so.

754
00:30:35.222 --> 00:30:42.806
<v DIGILORMO>So did people . . . So if there wasn't a barbershop here, did you mention that people would go to other people's houses?

755
00:30:42.806 --> 00:30:50.750
Like say there would be someone in the community that could cut hair and so they would do it out their house?

756
00:30:50.750 --> 00:30:52.194
Or just everybody went . . .?

757
00:30:52.194 --> 00:30:53.278
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah, probably so.

758
00:30:53.278 --> 00:30:54.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

759
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:54.392
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

760
00:30:54.392 --> 00:30:59.490
I'm pretty sure Mama . . . Daddy would take the boys to the barbershop, too.

761
00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:04.588
Sally and my mother didn't really have to do too much to theys.

762
00:31:04.588 --> 00:31:08.118
I'm the only one needed some special needs, so.

763
00:31:08.118 --> 00:31:08.510
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

764
00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:17.137
<v GAUTHIA>Them was always like maybe kinfolks mostly until after I got bigger and then I wanted to go get it professional done,

765
00:31:17.137 --> 00:31:18.706
but other than that . . .

766
00:31:18.706 --> 00:31:19.098
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

767
00:31:19.098 --> 00:31:19.490
Alright.

768
00:31:19.490 --> 00:31:24.196
Well so you mentioned that you graduated the last class of Mossville.

769
00:31:24.196 --> 00:31:24.980
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah, 1969.

770
00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:34.000
<v DIGILORMO>When that was going on, were you aware of how significant it was that you were part of that moment in history?

771
00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:35.524
<v GAUTHIA>Well, I don't know.

772
00:31:35.524 --> 00:31:39.333
<v DIGILORMO>I mean how'd people feel about the closing down of . . .?

773
00:31:39.333 --> 00:31:40.476
<v GAUTHIA>Of the school?

774
00:31:40.476 --> 00:31:40.857
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

775
00:31:40.857 --> 00:31:48.095
<v GAUTHIA>They had a lot of them voice their opinion, but I'm easygoing so I just go with the flow.

776
00:31:48.095 --> 00:31:52.667
I never was a person to, I guess say, buck the system.

777
00:31:52.667 --> 00:31:53.048
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

778
00:31:53.048 --> 00:31:57.238
<v GAUTHIA>If that's what they going to do it's okay with me.

779
00:31:57.238 --> 00:32:00.667
I'll just be in agreement to whatever going on.

780
00:32:00.667 --> 00:32:04.095
<v DIGILORMO>And it didn't affect you so much to where . . .

781
00:32:04.095 --> 00:32:04.476
<v GAUTHIA>No.

782
00:32:04.476 --> 00:32:06.000
<v DIGILORMO>It upset you.

783
00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:09.840
<v GAUTHIA>No. They had some that went to Westlake . . .

784
00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:10.320
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

785
00:32:10.320 --> 00:32:14.160
<v GAUTHIA>That left before the last class to graduate.

786
00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:14.640
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

787
00:32:14.640 --> 00:32:18.960
So the school was already starting to thin out.

788
00:32:18.960 --> 00:32:20.880
<v GAUTHIA>It was beginning . . . yeah.

789
00:32:20.880 --> 00:32:21.360
Yeah.

790
00:32:21.360 --> 00:32:25.680
They was trying to, I guess, blend it in.

791
00:32:25.680 --> 00:32:29.040
Some of them . . . Did go to Westlake.

792
00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:30.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

793
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.333
<v GAUTHIA>Some of my classmates.

794
00:32:31.333 --> 00:32:31.667
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

795
00:32:31.667 --> 00:32:35.333
<v GAUTHIA>So it wasn't a lot, but it was a small group.

796
00:32:35.333 --> 00:32:38.667
<v DIGILORMO>Did they start bringing white students in before you graduated?

797
00:32:38.667 --> 00:32:42.000
<v GAUTHIA>No. Just the blacks was going to the white school.

798
00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:42.333
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

799
00:32:42.333 --> 00:32:43.333
I got you.

800
00:32:43.333 --> 00:32:46.000
That wasn't until later when they started . . .

801
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:46.310
<v GAUTHIA>Right.

802
00:32:46.310 --> 00:32:46.621
Yeah.

803
00:32:46.621 --> 00:32:46.931
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

804
00:32:46.931 --> 00:32:52.207
So after you graduated, what type of work did you do or what was your life like?

805
00:32:52.207 --> 00:32:55.310
<v GAUTHIA>Well, I would just help my parents at the club.

806
00:32:55.310 --> 00:32:55.621
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

807
00:32:55.621 --> 00:32:57.172
<v GAUTHIA>Like, I didn't work out.

808
00:32:57.172 --> 00:32:58.724
Well I take that back.

809
00:32:58.724 --> 00:33:05.862
I did work at Holly Hill a little while and mama really didn't want me to go to work but I begged her.

810
00:33:05.862 --> 00:33:09.586
I said, “Mama I just want to go and receive a check.”

811
00:33:09.586 --> 00:33:12.379
Working for my parents you didn't receive no check.

812
00:33:12.379 --> 00:33:12.690
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

813
00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:16.103
<v GAUTHIA>And I can remember saying, "Mama, you can have my check.

814
00:33:16.103 --> 00:33:17.655
I don't want my check.

815
00:33:17.655 --> 00:33:19.828
I just want to have a check."

816
00:33:19.828 --> 00:33:20.138
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

817
00:33:20.138 --> 00:33:21.069
<v GAUTHIA>Just to say . . .

818
00:33:21.069 --> 00:33:22.000
<v DIGILORMO>Some independence.

819
00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:22.450
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

820
00:33:22.450 --> 00:33:27.846
And she let me go and I worked a little while there.

821
00:33:27.846 --> 00:33:29.644
So it was okay.

822
00:33:29.644 --> 00:33:34.141
You can come in, T. He's waiting to come in.

823
00:33:34.141 --> 00:33:35.940
You can come in.

824
00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:38.638
You're not going to hurt anything.

825
00:33:38.638 --> 00:33:39.087
Okay.

826
00:33:39.087 --> 00:33:41.336
I'm sorry keeping you outside.

827
00:33:41.336 --> 00:33:47.181
I seen a while ago you wanted to come in and I forgot.

828
00:33:47.181 --> 00:33:50.329
That's the little guy that lives here.

829
00:33:50.329 --> 00:33:50.779
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

830
00:33:50.779 --> 00:33:53.027
<v GAUTHIA>And he's a little weak.

831
00:33:53.027 --> 00:33:54.376
<v DIGILORMO>I got you.

832
00:33:54.376 --> 00:33:57.074
<c.p>“T”: My feet are killing me.

833
00:33:57.074 --> 00:34:03.819
They asked me this morning why my feet were [?] and I said I don’t know.

834
00:34:03.819 --> 00:34:06.517
<v GAUTHIA>Fluid . . . because your body holding fluid.

835
00:34:06.517 --> 00:34:06.966
Yeah.

836
00:34:06.966 --> 00:34:08.315
<c.p>“T”: They got [ . . .?].

837
00:34:08.315 --> 00:34:08.765
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

838
00:34:08.765 --> 00:34:09.664
Oh, yeah.

839
00:34:09.664 --> 00:34:16.409
Well maybe not to cross over, you do better go around, if you don't mind.

840
00:34:16.409 --> 00:34:18.208
He'll just go around.

841
00:34:18.208 --> 00:34:18.658
<v DIGILORMO>Alright.

842
00:34:18.658 --> 00:34:21.805
<v GAUTHIA>And we . . . The wind knocked that down.

843
00:34:21.805 --> 00:34:23.604
He'll pick it up.

844
00:34:23.604 --> 00:34:29.000
So let's see, what else are we going to talk about?

845
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:36.349
<v DIGILORMO>Well I have a little bit . . . A few questions I wanted to ask you about religion, things like that.

846
00:34:36.349 --> 00:34:38.283
You said you're a Catholic.

847
00:34:38.283 --> 00:34:38.670
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

848
00:34:38.670 --> 00:34:39.830
<v DIGILORMO>Your family's Catholic.

849
00:34:39.830 --> 00:34:45.245
How big of a role did religion play in your day to day life?

850
00:34:45.245 --> 00:34:51.047
<v GAUTHIA>I'm one of these . . . I love going to church and I'll go to anybody's church.

851
00:34:51.047 --> 00:34:56.849
I can remember one time that they didn't believe in people . . . If you was Catholic,

852
00:34:56.849 --> 00:35:00.330
they didn't want you to go out your church.

853
00:35:00.330 --> 00:35:02.264
<v DIGILORMO>The Catholics didn't or the . . .?

854
00:35:02.264 --> 00:35:03.425
<v GAUTHIA>No, the Catholics.

855
00:35:03.425 --> 00:35:03.811
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

856
00:35:03.811 --> 00:35:05.358
<v GAUTHIA>The Catholics, for sure.

857
00:35:05.358 --> 00:35:09.226
I didn't see no harm in it myself, you see.

858
00:35:09.226 --> 00:35:10.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

859
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:12.762
<v GAUTHIA>So now I tends to go to anybody's church.

860
00:35:12.762 --> 00:35:15.832
Somebody tell me they got church going on, I'm ready.

861
00:35:15.832 --> 00:35:22.891
I say, "If I can go, I'll try to go," if I can get somebody to watch my daddy and help my dad.

862
00:35:22.891 --> 00:35:23.198
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

863
00:35:23.198 --> 00:35:24.119
<v GAUTHIA>So I'd go.

864
00:35:24.119 --> 00:35:27.495
<v DIGILORMO>Did you ever have any problems going to Baptist, or Pentecostal,

865
00:35:27.495 --> 00:35:32.099
or any other types of churches when they . . . If they found out you were Catholic?

866
00:35:32.099 --> 00:35:34.554
<v GAUTHIA>No. That was way like, later you see.

867
00:35:34.554 --> 00:35:34.861
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

868
00:35:34.861 --> 00:35:36.396
<v GAUTHIA>No, that was way later.

869
00:35:36.396 --> 00:35:37.317
<v DIGILORMO>I got you.

870
00:35:37.317 --> 00:35:37.624
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

871
00:35:37.624 --> 00:35:41.000
<v DIGILORMO>So you've heard stories about that, or in previous generations?

872
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:43.638
<v GAUTHIA>I don't remember too much about it.

873
00:35:43.638 --> 00:35:44.014
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

874
00:35:44.014 --> 00:35:47.783
<v GAUTHIA>Because if my parents didn't care for us to go,

875
00:35:47.783 --> 00:35:54.942
because that if they didn't want you to go out of your church, that's what we had to do.

876
00:35:54.942 --> 00:35:55.319
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

877
00:35:55.319 --> 00:35:58.333
So both your parents were pretty spiritual people?

878
00:35:58.333 --> 00:36:02.855
Religious people that made sure y'all went to church and all that?

879
00:36:02.855 --> 00:36:03.232
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

880
00:36:03.232 --> 00:36:03.986
Oh yeah.

881
00:36:03.986 --> 00:36:07.000
Went to catechism and stuff like that.

882
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:07.404
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

883
00:36:07.404 --> 00:36:07.809
Yeah.

884
00:36:07.809 --> 00:36:10.638
How many days a week would you . . .?

885
00:36:10.638 --> 00:36:15.894
<v GAUTHIA>I think it was like one day a week you go to catechism.

886
00:36:15.894 --> 00:36:16.298
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

887
00:36:16.298 --> 00:36:16.702
Yeah.

888
00:36:16.702 --> 00:36:20.340
<v GAUTHIA>I think maybe they started out on a Saturday.

889
00:36:20.340 --> 00:36:21.149
<v DIGILORMO>Sounds right.

890
00:36:21.149 --> 00:36:21.553
Excellent.

891
00:36:21.553 --> 00:36:26.000
Well . . . So what was the Catholic Church in Westlake like?

892
00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:32.024
<v GAUTHIA>Well once they separated they . . . First we used to have to go to the black church.

893
00:36:32.024 --> 00:36:34.659
It was an all the black church.

894
00:36:34.659 --> 00:36:35.035
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

895
00:36:35.035 --> 00:36:43.318
<v GAUTHIA>Then they started letting us go to the big church and then we had to sit in the back of the church.

896
00:36:43.318 --> 00:36:46.706
Then the whites was . . . Would be in the front.

897
00:36:46.706 --> 00:36:47.459
<v DIGILORMO>What year?

898
00:36:47.459 --> 00:36:49.341
<v GAUTHIA>I don't remember the year.

899
00:36:49.341 --> 00:36:52.353
<v DIGILORMO>Would that have been in like the ‘70s?

900
00:36:52.353 --> 00:36:53.482
<v GAUTHIA>Oh, probably so.

901
00:36:53.482 --> 00:36:53.859
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

902
00:36:53.859 --> 00:36:54.235
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

903
00:36:54.235 --> 00:36:56.871
No, it probably was in the ‘60s.

904
00:36:56.871 --> 00:36:58.000
<v DIGILORMO>Oh, really?

905
00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:01.000
<v GAUTHIA>I would think in the ‘60s.

906
00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:05.500
<v DIGILORMO>So they didn't integrate the churches until after that?

907
00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:06.000
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

908
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:09.000
I don't remember what year.

909
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:09.370
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

910
00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:09.740
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

911
00:37:09.740 --> 00:37:11.961
<v DIGILORMO>And there were still two churches?

912
00:37:11.961 --> 00:37:14.182
Or did they shut down one?

913
00:37:14.182 --> 00:37:17.143
<v GAUTHIA>No, now we just got the one Catholic.

914
00:37:17.143 --> 00:37:18.253
<v DIGILORMO>Just the one?

915
00:37:18.253 --> 00:37:18.623
Okay.

916
00:37:18.623 --> 00:37:22.695
Are there a lot of congregants that are from Mossville there?

917
00:37:22.695 --> 00:37:23.065
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

918
00:37:23.065 --> 00:37:27.136
The Catholics still goes to . . . Well some goes to Sulphur [Louisiana].

919
00:37:27.136 --> 00:37:27.506
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

920
00:37:27.506 --> 00:37:29.727
<v GAUTHIA>Some even goes to Lake Charles.

921
00:37:29.727 --> 00:37:31.578
So I guess they just . . .

922
00:37:31.578 --> 00:37:32.318
<v DIGILORMO>Oh, wow.

923
00:37:32.318 --> 00:37:36.019
<v GAUTHIA>Now you got a preference to go wherever you choose.

924
00:37:36.019 --> 00:37:36.390
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

925
00:37:36.390 --> 00:37:43.792
<v GAUTHIA>Before, years ago, I think if you belonged to this area that's the church you had supposed to go to.

926
00:37:43.792 --> 00:37:48.974
I can remember I say, "Well I'll catch any church service that was available,"

927
00:37:48.974 --> 00:37:54.156
you see, because a lot of times I was working in my parents’ club.

928
00:37:54.156 --> 00:37:59.338
So on a Saturday night, it was the longest night you stayed open late.

929
00:37:59.338 --> 00:38:02.669
So I would prefer catching an afternoon service on

930
00:38:02.669 --> 00:38:03.039
<c.p>Sunday.

931
00:38:03.039 --> 00:38:03.409
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

932
00:38:03.409 --> 00:38:03.779
Yeah.

933
00:38:03.779 --> 00:38:06.000
<v GAUTHIA>So that's how that was.

934
00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:06.435
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

935
00:38:06.435 --> 00:38:15.130
Well . . . So was this church in Westlake involved in Mossville in any way even though it wasn't located in Mossville?

936
00:38:15.130 --> 00:38:24.261
Would they ever hold any type of activities or events here in Mossville to promote the church, or any sort of . . .?

937
00:38:24.261 --> 00:38:25.565
<v GAUTHIA>I don't remember.

938
00:38:25.565 --> 00:38:26.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

939
00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:28.609
So probably not a whole lot.

940
00:38:28.609 --> 00:38:30.783
<v GAUTHIA>No, I don't think so.

941
00:38:30.783 --> 00:38:36.435
I remember they used to . . . My parents would buy us donuts on Sunday.

942
00:38:36.435 --> 00:38:36.870
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

943
00:38:36.870 --> 00:38:42.957
<v GAUTHIA>They had a . . . They would sell donut after church and we'd always like that.

944
00:38:42.957 --> 00:38:43.391
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

945
00:38:43.391 --> 00:38:46.000
<v GAUTHIA>Get to get donuts! [laughs]

946
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:46.552
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

947
00:38:46.552 --> 00:38:54.836
<v GAUTHIA>So that was one of our, I guess, highlights to go to church, you see.

948
00:38:54.836 --> 00:38:55.388
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

949
00:38:55.388 --> 00:38:57.045
I see that.

950
00:38:57.045 --> 00:39:00.910
Where there any weddings in the church?

951
00:39:00.910 --> 00:39:04.224
Or funerals for people of Mossville?

952
00:39:04.224 --> 00:39:10.299
<v GAUTHIA>Probably . . . Back years ago was probably having them in the homes.

953
00:39:10.299 --> 00:39:10.851
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

954
00:39:10.851 --> 00:39:13.612
<v GAUTHIA>The funerals in the home.

955
00:39:13.612 --> 00:39:16.373
Probably weddings, too, I guess.

956
00:39:16.373 --> 00:39:23.000
<v DIGILORMO>Do you have any memories of any specific or special occasions?

957
00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:25.043
<v GAUTHIA>I can't remember right now.

958
00:39:25.043 --> 00:39:25.452
No.

959
00:39:25.452 --> 00:39:25.860
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

960
00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:29.538
No big weddings in somebody's home that you can . . .?

961
00:39:29.538 --> 00:39:38.527
<v GAUTHIA>Well I can remember my parents, when the kids would get married, my siblings, they believed in giving them a little wedding.

962
00:39:38.527 --> 00:39:42.613
They would give after the . . . In the hall; the dance

963
00:39:42.613 --> 00:39:43.022
<c.p>hall.

964
00:39:43.022 --> 00:39:43.430
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

965
00:39:43.430 --> 00:39:49.151
<v GAUTHIA>So I didn't care for that because I'm kind of, prefer just plain simple.

966
00:39:49.151 --> 00:39:54.054
So I didn't tell my parents I was getting married and stuff.

967
00:39:54.054 --> 00:40:01.000
They probably assumed I would because I had talked to my husband a long time, but.

968
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:01.347
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

969
00:40:01.347 --> 00:40:03.776
When you say the hall you mean . . .

970
00:40:03.776 --> 00:40:04.816
<v GAUTHIA>The dance hall.

971
00:40:04.816 --> 00:40:05.510
<v DIGILORMO>The club?

972
00:40:05.510 --> 00:40:05.857
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

973
00:40:05.857 --> 00:40:08.980
Well they had the dance hall and the club.

974
00:40:08.980 --> 00:40:09.327
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

975
00:40:09.327 --> 00:40:13.490
<v GAUTHIA>They club was kind of separated where they go every day there.

976
00:40:13.490 --> 00:40:17.306
Then the dance hall is only when they had special function.

977
00:40:17.306 --> 00:40:18.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

978
00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:18.706
<v GAUTHIA>You see.

979
00:40:18.706 --> 00:40:19.059
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

980
00:40:19.059 --> 00:40:22.235
They would rent it out and do wedding receptions.

981
00:40:22.235 --> 00:40:22.588
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

982
00:40:22.588 --> 00:40:22.941
Whatever.

983
00:40:22.941 --> 00:40:23.294
Yeah.

984
00:40:23.294 --> 00:40:23.647
Entertainment.

985
00:40:23.647 --> 00:40:24.353
Special entertainments.

986
00:40:24.353 --> 00:40:24.706
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

987
00:40:24.706 --> 00:40:25.412
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah, so.

988
00:40:25.412 --> 00:40:27.529
<v DIGILORMO>So what happened to the club?

989
00:40:27.529 --> 00:40:29.647
Why did it get shut down?

990
00:40:29.647 --> 00:40:35.294
<v GAUTHIA>I would assume my parents were getting where they were kind of getting tired of it.

991
00:40:35.294 --> 00:40:36.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

992
00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:38.872
<v GAUTHIA>My daddy had done already retired from the plant.

993
00:40:38.872 --> 00:40:43.979
It just . . . And by then my mom and them had done built this new house here.

994
00:40:43.979 --> 00:40:46.213
So then it wasn't in walking distance.

995
00:40:46.213 --> 00:40:50.681
Well it was walking distance, but not like in the same yard, you see.

996
00:40:50.681 --> 00:40:51.000
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

997
00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.553
<v GAUTHIA>They had a good little piece to walk.

998
00:40:53.553 --> 00:40:58.340
So I guess they just kind of got tired and decided to shut it down.

999
00:40:58.340 --> 00:40:58.660
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1000
00:40:58.660 --> 00:41:02.170
So they didn't sell it to try to keep it going.

1001
00:41:02.170 --> 00:41:02.809
They just . . .

1002
00:41:02.809 --> 00:41:04.723
<v GAUTHIA>I think they just closed it.

1003
00:41:04.723 --> 00:41:05.362
<v DIGILORMO>Closed it.

1004
00:41:05.362 --> 00:41:06.000
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1005
00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:06.460
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1006
00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:06.920
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1007
00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:07.380
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1008
00:41:07.380 --> 00:41:10.140
Did he own any other clubs?

1009
00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:10.600
<v GAUTHIA>No.

1010
00:41:10.600 --> 00:41:12.440
<v DIGILORMO>Okay, just that one.

1011
00:41:12.440 --> 00:41:12.900
<v GAUTHIA>[Agrees].

1012
00:41:12.900 --> 00:41:13.360
<v DIGILORMO>Alright.

1013
00:41:13.360 --> 00:41:19.800
That must have been kind of hard to watch that piece of Mossville go.

1014
00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:28.080
<v GAUTHIA>Oh no. We was . . . No. I guess everybody was kind of . . . tired and was ready for it to . . .

1015
00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:29.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1016
00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:32.794
<v GAUTHIA>I guess the excitement kind of was going away.

1017
00:41:32.794 --> 00:41:36.588
Because my parents, them wasn't giving the dance halls.

1018
00:41:36.588 --> 00:41:38.696
Those big entertainment anymore, so.

1019
00:41:38.696 --> 00:41:39.118
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

1020
00:41:39.118 --> 00:41:45.020
<v GAUTHIA>They just kind of eventually just kind of, for whatever reason shut it down.

1021
00:41:45.020 --> 00:41:45.441
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1022
00:41:45.441 --> 00:41:53.451
Well so growing up where would you have received medical treatment or attention if you got sick, or hurt?

1023
00:41:53.451 --> 00:41:55.559
Was there somewhere around here?

1024
00:41:55.559 --> 00:42:01.039
Or did you pretty much have to go to Lake Charles or something?

1025
00:42:01.039 --> 00:42:05.676
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah you had to go either to Sulphur or Lake Charles.

1026
00:42:05.676 --> 00:42:10.314
And if you didn't have insurance you go to Moss Regional.

1027
00:42:10.314 --> 00:42:11.157
<v DIGILORMO>Moss Regional?

1028
00:42:11.157 --> 00:42:12.000
<v GAUTHIA>[Agrees]

1029
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:12.365
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1030
00:42:12.365 --> 00:42:14.192
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah that's the charity hospital.

1031
00:42:14.192 --> 00:42:21.863
I can remember when I got married I didn't have any insurance because I was . . . I guess I got too old.

1032
00:42:21.863 --> 00:42:25.881
My parents . . . I got dropped from the insurance after a while.

1033
00:42:25.881 --> 00:42:26.247
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

1034
00:42:26.247 --> 00:42:30.630
<v GAUTHIA>I got pregnant after a couple of years after I was married.

1035
00:42:30.630 --> 00:42:34.283
And I didn't have no insurance and I was pregnant.

1036
00:42:34.283 --> 00:42:39.397
And I can remember this and I just thought my daddy was so special.

1037
00:42:39.397 --> 00:42:40.858
He had told me.

1038
00:42:40.858 --> 00:42:48.895
He says, "Judy, since you don't have no insurance, I don't want you to go have your baby at Moss Regional Charity."

1039
00:42:48.895 --> 00:42:52.913
He said, "Because they don't give you medicine when you hurting.

1040
00:42:52.913 --> 00:42:54.740
They just let you suffer."

1041
00:42:54.740 --> 00:43:01.315
He said, "I'm going to send you to the pay hospital, and I'm going to pay for it."

1042
00:43:01.315 --> 00:43:07.890
He said, "Even if I don't have the money I'll make a loan and see that you go."

1043
00:43:07.890 --> 00:43:10.813
To a pay hospital to have my baby.

1044
00:43:10.813 --> 00:43:18.849
I was fortunate, God blessed me that my husband was a veteran and they sent me some insurance and I was covered,

1045
00:43:18.849 --> 00:43:26.521
so my parents didn't have to send me to a pay hospital and I didn't have to go to Moss Regional.

1046
00:43:26.521 --> 00:43:27.982
<v DIGILORMO>Wow, that's a blessing.

1047
00:43:27.982 --> 00:43:28.347
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1048
00:43:28.347 --> 00:43:30.904
And I still have my insurance today.

1049
00:43:30.904 --> 00:43:31.269
<v DIGILORMO>Nice.

1050
00:43:31.269 --> 00:43:32.000
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1051
00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:35.341
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah, it can be a mess without it.

1052
00:43:35.341 --> 00:43:35.758
<v GAUTHIA>Yes.

1053
00:43:35.758 --> 00:43:42.857
<v DIGILORMO>So was there anyone . . . Say you didn't have like a real bad illness or anything like that,

1054
00:43:42.857 --> 00:43:50.374
but there was something maybe sore throat, or headaches, was there anyone in the area that treated people?

1055
00:43:50.374 --> 00:43:57.055
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah they . . . I can remember my parents taking us to people and they would treat us.

1056
00:43:57.055 --> 00:44:01.231
Instead of go to the doctor we we’d go there.

1057
00:44:01.231 --> 00:44:01.648
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

1058
00:44:01.648 --> 00:44:03.736
<v GAUTHIA>And he would heal us.

1059
00:44:03.736 --> 00:44:04.154
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1060
00:44:04.154 --> 00:44:06.659
<v GAUTHIA>For headaches, stomach aches, worms, whatever.

1061
00:44:06.659 --> 00:44:10.000
<v DIGILORMO>Do you remember any of the treatments?

1062
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:11.200
<v GAUTHIA>I don't remember.

1063
00:44:11.200 --> 00:44:13.200
They would pray over us.

1064
00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:13.600
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1065
00:44:13.600 --> 00:44:21.200
<v GAUTHIA>Or sometime, I can remember they telling us take some garlic and wear it around your waist or something.

1066
00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:24.800
Kind of keep the worms away . . . something like that.

1067
00:44:24.800 --> 00:44:26.400
I don't remember how.

1068
00:44:26.400 --> 00:44:26.800
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1069
00:44:26.800 --> 00:44:29.600
<v GAUTHIA>But I remember something about the garlic.

1070
00:44:29.600 --> 00:44:30.400
<v DIGILORMO>The garlic.

1071
00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:31.200
That's interesting.

1072
00:44:31.200 --> 00:44:32.000
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1073
00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:35.291
<v DIGILORMO>Do you remember . . . I mean I know you probably were a small child,

1074
00:44:35.291 --> 00:44:38.582
but in your memory did it ever work or make you feel better?

1075
00:44:38.582 --> 00:44:39.848
<v GAUTHIA>I think it would work.

1076
00:44:39.848 --> 00:44:40.101
Yeah.

1077
00:44:40.101 --> 00:44:40.354
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1078
00:44:40.354 --> 00:44:40.608
Wow.

1079
00:44:40.608 --> 00:44:42.886
<v GAUTHIA>Because that's the only place we had to go.

1080
00:44:42.886 --> 00:44:43.139
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

1081
00:44:43.139 --> 00:44:44.658
<v GAUTHIA>So I'm pretty sure it worked.

1082
00:44:44.658 --> 00:44:50.228
<v DIGILORMO>Were there quite a few people or just like one or two in the community that had these sort of . . . the knowledge?

1083
00:44:50.228 --> 00:44:52.000
<v GAUTHIA>No, it wasn't a whole lot.

1084
00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:52.404
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1085
00:44:52.404 --> 00:44:55.640
<v GAUTHIA>No, everybody would go to the same one.

1086
00:44:55.640 --> 00:44:56.045
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1087
00:44:56.045 --> 00:44:56.449
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1088
00:44:56.449 --> 00:44:59.685
<v DIGILORMO>Do you remember any names by any chance?

1089
00:44:59.685 --> 00:45:03.730
I mean I'm sure they may not be around anymore.

1090
00:45:03.730 --> 00:45:07.775
<v GAUTHIA>No. They not around, but I don't remember the name.

1091
00:45:07.775 --> 00:45:08.180
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1092
00:45:08.180 --> 00:45:19.910
<v GAUTHIA>And sometime they would go in the woods and they knew certain herbs and they would go get that and boil that and give us certain herbs to take.

1093
00:45:19.910 --> 00:45:21.933
I remember that mamou tea.

1094
00:45:21.933 --> 00:45:23.146
Sassafras tea, so.

1095
00:45:23.146 --> 00:45:23.551
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1096
00:45:23.551 --> 00:45:28.000
Is that spelled the same way as Mamou, the town?

1097
00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.067
<v GAUTHIA>I think so.

1098
00:45:29.067 --> 00:45:29.779
Probably so.

1099
00:45:29.779 --> 00:45:30.846
I don't know.

1100
00:45:30.846 --> 00:45:33.336
<v DIGILORMO>I wonder if it comes from there.

1101
00:45:33.336 --> 00:45:34.403
<v GAUTHIA>I don't know.

1102
00:45:34.403 --> 00:45:35.114
<v DIGILORMO>That's interesting.

1103
00:45:35.114 --> 00:45:36.537
What about your parents?

1104
00:45:36.537 --> 00:45:42.228
Did they ever have any like little remedies around the house for stuff like sore throat?

1105
00:45:42.228 --> 00:45:48.987
I mean maybe not as extensive as going and searching for herbs, but just little whatever in the house?

1106
00:45:48.987 --> 00:45:55.034
<v GAUTHIA>Well my parents always kept anything that would . . . They felt like we needed for . . . to be sick.

1107
00:45:55.034 --> 00:45:56.456
So I don't remember.

1108
00:45:56.456 --> 00:45:57.168
Cough syrup.

1109
00:45:57.168 --> 00:45:58.235
Oh, the Watkins.

1110
00:45:58.235 --> 00:46:03.215
They used to . . . I can remember people would sell Watkins out of they car.

1111
00:46:03.215 --> 00:46:05.705
And they would come in the communities

1112
00:46:05.705 --> 00:46:10.329
<c.p>and stop by different houses to see if you wanted to buy anything.

1113
00:46:10.329 --> 00:46:18.154
They'd have it in the trunk of they car, or inside they car, and you’d go look and see what you want.

1114
00:46:18.154 --> 00:46:19.221
<v DIGILORMO>And what is . . .?

1115
00:46:19.221 --> 00:46:20.289
<v GAUTHIA>Like cough syrups.

1116
00:46:20.289 --> 00:46:21.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1117
00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:27.147
<v GAUTHIA>Rubs . . . to rub your knee or whatever type thing like that.

1118
00:46:27.147 --> 00:46:30.500
<v DIGILORMO>And what did you call them?

1119
00:46:30.500 --> 00:46:31.059
<v GAUTHIA>Watkins.

1120
00:46:31.059 --> 00:46:31.618
<v DIGILORMO>W-A-K?

1121
00:46:31.618 --> 00:46:32.176
<v GAUTHIA>K-I-N.

1122
00:46:32.176 --> 00:46:37.765
Might be apostrophe S. And it's still around today, Watkins.

1123
00:46:37.765 --> 00:46:38.324
<v DIGILORMO>Really?

1124
00:46:38.324 --> 00:46:40.000
That's interesting.

1125
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:48.966
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah they got a place in Sulphur that has a sign that says, “Watkins,” that they sell Watkins out the home.

1126
00:46:48.966 --> 00:46:49.393
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1127
00:46:49.393 --> 00:46:52.382
Well I'll have to look into that.

1128
00:46:52.382 --> 00:46:52.809
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1129
00:46:52.809 --> 00:46:54.944
<v DIGILORMO>Never heard of that before.

1130
00:46:54.944 --> 00:46:56.652
Okay, well let's see.

1131
00:46:56.652 --> 00:47:00.921
Got a few questions about just the community in general.

1132
00:47:00.921 --> 00:47:05.191
If you personally . . . And there's no right or wrong answer.

1133
00:47:05.191 --> 00:47:05.618
<v GAUTHIA>Okay.

1134
00:47:05.618 --> 00:47:14.157
<v DIGILORMO>But if you personally had to name the boundaries, the geographical boundaries, of Mossville what would you say they were?

1135
00:47:14.157 --> 00:47:18.000
I mean you could use streets, or buildings . . .

1136
00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:21.360
<v GAUTHIA>Well the end of Prater Road.

1137
00:47:21.360 --> 00:47:24.160
That was like Mossville to . . .

1138
00:47:24.160 --> 00:47:26.960
<v DIGILORMO>Where it hits [Highway] 90.

1139
00:47:26.960 --> 00:47:29.200
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah, 90 to Prater.

1140
00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:39.280
And in Sulphur I would say off of Old Spanish Trail all the way . . . They have Evergreen Road.

1141
00:47:39.280 --> 00:47:42.640
That was considered like Mossville, too.

1142
00:47:42.640 --> 00:47:48.240
And then you go until Westlake past the school house.

1143
00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:50.480
That would be Mossville.

1144
00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:51.040
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1145
00:47:51.040 --> 00:47:51.600
Okay.

1146
00:47:51.600 --> 00:47:57.200
Yeah and I guess Westlake would be north of Mossville.

1147
00:47:57.200 --> 00:47:58.880
All back there?

1148
00:47:58.880 --> 00:48:00.000
<v GAUTHIA>[Agrees].

1149
00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:00.407
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1150
00:48:00.407 --> 00:48:00.813
Interesting.

1151
00:48:00.813 --> 00:48:06.505
So what do you know about the names of the streets here in Mossville?

1152
00:48:06.505 --> 00:48:13.418
<v GAUTHIA>Well, they got a Moss Avenue and I'm assuming they had an elderly family, they was Mosses.

1153
00:48:13.418 --> 00:48:18.297
And I think that's how they got some of they names from.

1154
00:48:18.297 --> 00:48:22.769
So I don't know too much about that history like that.

1155
00:48:22.769 --> 00:48:23.176
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1156
00:48:23.176 --> 00:48:28.868
It does seem like a lot of the names are named after prominent families . . .

1157
00:48:28.868 --> 00:48:29.275
<v GAUTHIA>Yeah.

1158
00:48:29.275 --> 00:48:30.495
<v DIGILORMO>Here in Mossville.

1159
00:48:30.495 --> 00:48:35.374
Which it seems like there should almost be a Montgomery Avenue somewhere.

1160
00:48:35.374 --> 00:48:35.780
<v GAUTHIA>Right.

1161
00:48:35.780 --> 00:48:37.000
Right. [laughs]

1162
00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:39.110
<v DIGILORMO>How do we petition for that? [laughs]

1163
00:48:39.110 --> 00:48:40.014
<v GAUTHIA>I don't know.

1164
00:48:40.014 --> 00:48:42.425
